      <h2>Who Benefits Most from Cognitive Shuffling?</h2>
      <p>
        Cognitive Shuffling is particularly powerful for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Bedtime Ruminators:</strong> Individuals whose primary sleep complaint is replaying social interactions or worrying about upcoming challenges.</li>
        <li><strong>Nighttime Awakening:</strong> People who wake up at 2 AM or 3 AM with sudden mental alertness.</li>
        <li><strong>Shift Workers and Travelers:</strong> Those trying to sleep outside their natural circadian window who need to artificially lower cortical arousal.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="guide-disclaimer">
        <strong>Wellness Notice:</strong> Cognitive Shuffling is a behavioral sleep-hygiene tool and non-clinical mental exercise. It is not intended as a replacement for clinical treatment of chronic insomnia disorder, sleep apnea, or clinical anxiety disorders. If severe sleep disruption persists, consult a qualified medical professional.
      </div>

